\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces GES components against chemical potential at $T=0.1\,\mathrm  {meV}$. Top: near the van Hove energy (dashed vertical line). Bottom: high-density side. Orange shading: geometry-driven ferromagnetic fluctuation ($\chi _{e}<0<\chi _{\rm  mass}$). Grey: dispersion-driven ($\chi _{e}<0$, $\chi _{\rm  mass}<0$).}}{5}{figure.caption.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:gesmu}{{3}{5}{GES components against chemical potential at $T=0.1\meV $. Top: near the van Hove energy (dashed vertical line). Bottom: high-density side. Orange shading: geometry-driven ferromagnetic fluctuation ($\chie <0<\chim $). Grey: dispersion-driven ($\chie <0$, $\chim <0$)}{figure.caption.6}{}}
